course: dictionary
lesson: 7191
title: A Latin word with two faces
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «Pes» is a Latin word, from an old language, so you will mostly meet it in science books. It means the foot: the foot part of an animal's back leg, or the foot in a medical name like «pes planus», which means flat foot.
explain: Context gives you the clues. If the sentence is about bones, feet or animals, «pes» probably means a foot. If the sentence is about a school timetable, «PEs» probably means PE lessons. Check by swapping in your meaning: "The dog's flat foot hurt" makes sense, so the meaning fits.
explain: Be careful: «pes» sounds like «pess», not «pest», which means an annoying animal or insect. Also, in some other languages, such as Czech, «pes» means dog, as in «pes» and «sobaka» both mean dog. Context tells you which meaning is right.
fact: «Pes» is a Latin word meaning foot.
fact: «Pes planus» means flat foot, and «pes cavus» means high arch.
fact: The plural of «pes» is «pedes».
fact: «PEs», written with a capital P and E and a small s, can mean PE lessons. It is a short form, not Latin.
fact: «Pes» is not the English word «pest».
exercise: «The horse's back pes was strong and steady.» In a science book, what does pes mean? | A kind of dog | A PE lesson | *The foot | A pest that bites
exercise: «The doctor said Sam has pes planus.» What is pes planus? | A school lesson | *A flat foot | A Latin dog | A high arch
exercise: Sam's timetable says «Monday: PEs, 2 o'clock.» What might PEs mean here? | Pest control | Pedes, the plural of a Latin word | *PE lessons | A dog show
test: Which English word sounds like «pes» but means something else? | Foot | Pedal | *Pest | Lesson
test: «Pes» is a word from which language? | *Latin | Scots | English | French
exam: Read: «The vet checked the pes of the injured dog.» What is pes most likely about? | A pest that bites | A word in Scots | *A foot | A PE lesson
